  "name": "setting-up-a-data-warehouse-source",
  "description": "Guide the user through connecting a new data warehouse source, including databases, SaaS tools, and bucket files. Use when the user wants to \"connect Stripe\", \"import data from Postgres\", \"import files from a bucket\", \"upload a file\", \"add a new data source\", or pick sync methods for each table. This skill covers source-type discovery, credential validation, table discovery, per-table sync_type selection, and the final create call. Also covers picking a good prefix, what to do right after creation, and sending a source's tables to the user's own warehouse (Snowflake, BigQuery, Postgres, S3 and other destinations).",
